{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30640 - PROTEIN:6147",
  "verbalization": "Alpneumine H is implicated in the target pathway leading to Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9 through a series of intermediate targets, including Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, and others like Flavipin and Michaolide J. These intermediates are all part of the same biological network, suggesting a potential functional link between Alpneumine H and the SDR family member. The evidence points to a mechanism where Alpneumine H may act as a modulator or activator of these targets, which in turn interact with the SDR family member. The shared involvement of thioredoxin and its downstream targets implies a possible role in redox regulation or metabolic processes, which could explain the observed relationship. The integration of multiple pathways supports the idea that Alpneumine H influences the activity of the SDR family member through a network of interconnected targets, highlighting a complex but coherent biological mechanism.",
